<header><p class="st-kicker">prince bishopric · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Prince-Bishopric of Halberstadt</h1><p class="st-meta">1180 CE – 1648 CE (approx.) · capital Halberstadt</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Church principality in the northern Harz foreland, founded under Charlemagne and secularised to Brandenburg at the Peace of Westphalia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The diocese of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halberstadt">Halberstadt</a> was founded about 804 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a> to christianise the eastern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/saxons">Saxons</a>. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> gathered counties and estates in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harz">Harz</a> foreland. After the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a> in 1180 freed them from his ducal power, they ruled a consolidated territory as imperial princes.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The cathedral chapter elected the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>, who ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/halberstadt">Halberstadt</a> and towns such as Gröningen. Its Gothic cathedral and treasury are among the richest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. From the 16th century the see was held by princes of the houses of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albert-of-brandenburg">Albert of Brandenburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-julius-duke-of-brunswick-luneburg">Henry Julius of Brunswick-Wolfenbüttel</a>, and the territory became Lutheran. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years War its administrator, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christian-the-younger-of-brunswick">Christian of Brunswick</a>, fought for the Protestant side.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a> in 1648 the see was secularised and given to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-halberstadt">Principality of Halberstadt</a>. It remained Prussian, apart from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-westphalia">Kingdom of Westphalia</a> interlude, and is now in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="prince bishopric, 1180 CE – 1648 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M30 82 V46 Q50 12 70 46 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 30 V82 M40 58 H60"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">prince bishopric</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:83.18%;width:9.31%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1180 CE – 1648 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>prince bishopric</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Halberstadt</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Albert of Brandenburg, Henry Julius of Brunswick-Wolfenbüttel, Christian of Brunswick</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism, then Lutheranism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Low German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hochstift Halberstadt</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1414&amp;focus=prince-bishopric-of-halberstadt" aria-label="Prince-Bishopric of Halberstadt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4929 384 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Prince-Bishopric of Halberstadt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5249 640L5229 694M5249 640L5249 640"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5229 694h0M5249 640h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5249 640h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5249 640h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Halberstadt. <a href="/atlas?year=1414&amp;focus=prince-bishopric-of-halberstadt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
